<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mian Nur Muhammad Kalhoro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1755</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mian Nur Muhammad Kalhoro was the most powerful ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalhora-dynasty">Kalhora dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a>, governing from 1719 until his death in 1755. He extended Kalhora control over almost all of the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a> valley but had to submit to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> in 1739 and later paid tribute to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-shah-abdali">Ahmad Shah Durrani</a>. His reign saw new irrigation canals and the patronage of Sindhi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufism">Sufi</a> poets.</p></div>
